[{"id":"VRCE-7-49-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":1,"english":"Beholding the great ascetic Vālmīki thus conducting Sītā into his own hermitage Lakş mana's heart was bewildered with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.554,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5733e9dfd87e24885bfe696ba9500441537b92b8c7de6b5822128b56a87ffff","compact":"dc002c2b44e078dfedb83867dd7363075ab2b49a09e5f2e3edf7c0529eda12a2","nasal":"dc002c2b44e078dfedb83867dd7363075ab2b49a09e5f2e3edf7c0529eda12a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":2,"english":"Thereupon he said to the expert charioteer Sumantra. Do you perceive Rāma's grief consequent upon the separation from Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.762,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"777deb33efa3001ff320c292f3042f1988adfcb36ef67386e65298d25d2c8d32","compact":"448bf9948abbb1f853a18e1b940a4cc7bd5b8594aba2806b8e9ec703066faacf","nasal":"de884f3b4ed20ce3adcf2e0cf6eb673dc9908023c789f9d377eb074f39073edc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":3,"english":"His spouse-the daughter of Janaka, is perfectly pure; what can be more painful than that Rāma is living alone having renounced her?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2572cc248ad28edb3765b992562784791e5ea7038d23af8404ef381719a3c99c","compact":"bc7d08f4ca29de84e72e9b746efedd78f3987e4cce29ed4c3df1dc206ded644c","nasal":"bc7d08f4ca29de84e72e9b746efedd78f3987e4cce29ed4c3df1dc206ded644c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":4,"english":"It is clear to me, O Sumantra, that this separation of Rāma, has been brought about by the influence of destiny-for it is hard to get over accident.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdd468dee5aa9b248e4c1fd606d49f91738905c911dcb616674ebb5d4b724c41","compact":"06b6d9462cb8b588b607da5e126729d6435d1de4e1ad474ec29d151e5e09c8f4","nasal":"06b6d9462cb8b588b607da5e126729d6435d1de4e1ad474ec29d151e5e09c8f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":5,"english":"Even that Rāma, who, when enraged, is capable of slaying the celestials, Gandharvas, Asuras and Rākşasas, has been engaged in the worship of destiny.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"415c103075f9684d2005d07d19b329f83cb1f21f16b841d77cf213ff25813951","compact":"0cecfdfe0ff1eb4833766475c3ae7fcf1260b3eb8daed3eff85a91cc99fd9e35","nasal":"12a6f6dd1b91d9ba6d9e4b4ac0a31b92fb35db83429a90a3bd2f1f78a62ce99d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":6,"english":"Formerly did Rāma go through miserics, residing in the forest of Dandaka, at the command of his sire for fourteen years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.446,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb809c1ee1df297c0923228cda94250af2e77c4a582c94e5c3553e41957bfe77","compact":"0c20aa42a86b2ab8621151a52b68ac6a6daf563bfabb4069b15c5562ebaf8c12","nasal":"c711ecc8bb8c2f80fa7979c07f4815051d727e02cc35c05cf61902513815cc06"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":7,"english":"But this banishment of Sītā appears to me as exceedingly painful and most ruthless. O charioteer, the opinion of the citizens is by no means just; consequently what shall we gain by performing such a bad action for fame as the exile of Sita?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d6e0ca60ebfe3992d02055e99a0a12141a8c367740225fc71ef63f0a96c16ac","compact":"0f0c52845807baf3a1a31072f4d4dde97e7531a9ab452b28183bb6a18c9f0ea4","nasal":"7e23ae2f1e2add7da25a29c2f6807b1a30fabcfe162becd8462ddbae949f5899"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":8,"english":"But this banishment of Sītā appears to me as exceedingly painful and most ruthless. O charioteer, the opinion of the citizens is by no means just; consequently what shall we gain by performing such a bad action for fame as the exile of Sita?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.62,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e143de37148fb7665ea6a3721f87c55299892e64654c130f09c2611e37661d01","compact":"a75bbf4bfa0bdfeef31ebc6748f44f43db11314801630b5981be69a582eafaad","nasal":"a75bbf4bfa0bdfeef31ebc6748f44f43db11314801630b5981be69a582eafaad"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":9,"english":"Hearing those words of Lakşmaņa of various types, the wise Sumantra reverentially replied.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ee8a6dc32be229a7b9183f95f82dabcb6961a12f5cfc085ca8befa8ee7b798c","compact":"bb7023ebcef97b50addd2e6bde7102f90ec571669e4e0584162b9f3babaef95e","nasal":"6b07a36f99cc28f405786d22bdc054a30151096479cef5e76f2e2230a9b9b999"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":10,"english":"Be not aggrieved for Sītā, O Saumitri Formerly in the presence of your sire the Brāhmaṇas related this account of Sītā's exile.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa1559af7247459733371e7e826516017a5f7a5a0d5fe931df6f6597ff33012d","compact":"dd5ce0c542d5092933f9962706eeea92345a2f84ea721612fc4952c8221bd2f8","nasal":"dd5ce0c542d5092933f9962706eeea92345a2f84ea721612fc4952c8221bd2f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":11,"english":"Rāma shall be deprived of all happiness and be separated from his dear wife; what more, the virtuous-souled Rāma, having long arms, shall, under the influence of time, renounce you, Sītā, Śatrughna and Bharata.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.657,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae1c3763fb34820005ce4bc3304bc5dfc208adb8ccbcb886b5866c77428f6241","compact":"663f3bcc0a2c284aa491281850d2970a64b21aee3fe4d2ca920984c746ef4a72","nasal":"63fa374ac15b7b0483cb0566fd4385d31d67b8f0b0dc0800cabfec60635fcb29"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":12,"english":"O Lakṣmaṇa, when Durvāsa was addressed by the king Dasaratha as to your future he replied in the above way. I have told you the same. Do you not communicate this to Śatrughna Bharata or any body. O foremost of men, Durbasa said this to Daſaratha before me, Vaşistha and other great men.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.924,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39a7ac06a186b46c7da62384628468c897914ddb498f5a9efd4f1d668533a566","compact":"b36ebaad80c22e54e3a59fcc91176435f07f96d0e131b25f47617ce82c8672cc","nasal":"b36ebaad80c22e54e3a59fcc91176435f07f96d0e131b25f47617ce82c8672cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":13,"english":"O Lakṣmaṇa, when Durvāsa was addressed by the king Dasaratha as to your future he replied in the above way. I have told you the same. Do you not communicate this to Śatrughna Bharata or any body. O foremost of men, Durbasa said this to Daſaratha before me, Vaşistha and other great men.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b30a9575d67325a40247f5269925c2bff9bfda23f6e052156f6df0763ea16c2","compact":"17eb7137f9ec58429e062dc899e160807c9683759f2f783d78271de46e3208d3","nasal":"17eb7137f9ec58429e062dc899e160807c9683759f2f783d78271de46e3208d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing the words of Rsi, Dasaratha, the foremost of men, said to me, \"O charioteer, do not reveal this secret to any body.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6dbc819dd9042d0f32fbcfe5028b9f8deb5b648e9f59009972b3aa8d12661c5b","compact":"3d6fe1bf8c1d259aaa303a81ef75512669d3f45756f25fa1bbd6d71083446252","nasal":"3d6fe1bf8c1d259aaa303a81ef75512669d3f45756f25fa1bbd6d71083446252"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":15,"english":"O gentle one, it is not proper by any means to falsify the words of the king Dasaratha. I shall always, very carefully, carry out his orders. It is not proper to reveal this mystery before you. Still I do so for your curiosity has been greatly excited.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d0551fd67104ad25e1cf26d1570c96f9f71ac66d50fca257c27d7b19029a6f1","compact":"6e6a8ad0f8ef3e99b5754af2e5ca8831cd26aaeb7ebc514049e63dbdfb5706d1","nasal":"6e6a8ad0f8ef3e99b5754af2e5ca8831cd26aaeb7ebc514049e63dbdfb5706d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":16,"english":"O gentle one, it is not proper by any means to falsify the words of the king Dasaratha. I shall always, very carefully, carry out his orders. It is not proper to reveal this mystery before you. Still I do so for your curiosity has been greatly excited.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e86593d1eaa248e968dd7af9d2fcb7e0bf25604aeff42a8210b1bbf8fd7d805c","compact":"c6fe60c7c0748d31f2f0a0ca7cc99ed8ec29dedd50a53b6acaf8d6b8fcb64c35","nasal":"9457ffed541891738f164d8bb8301e2d5270128d3028544496166562b659aff8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":17,"english":"Tough this mystery was communicated formerly by the king Dasaratha and though it is not proper to reveal it to any body, still I express it before you that you may not, on hearing it, be worked up with sorrow; for destiny is hard to be got over. And it is by the influence of that destiny that you have met with such a sorrow and grief. However, do you not reveal this secret to Satrughna and Bharata.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.761,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39003645788647e6035945445833627b2680e6276b65222628656f3cdb1500a4","compact":"7c32334c0362bb9950c2a7f12bd415c50276766c5f868bc9f6f588cd00af1788","nasal":"d4bfae3513a78a5f552de11326e7070b7863bb27d6bff0b6445db04f279caa33"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-49-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":49,"verse":18,"english":"Hearing these grave and important words of Sumantra, Laksmana ordered him to relate.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-50-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7049018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"17b1f559adc5cf1e6ac91bcef54915a01fdd67ce3c536d93a7dcdce7326a25c5","compact":"aa8ef488425c24d86d439d5792303a6f1b73eeed0fa92cf8bb9734506f491b61","nasal":"4262d7668b5f3e0127a97c4f74e36ce750151b4fcaf090008d54f8733bc178f3"}}]
